['|Case|:user_login\n```\nFUNCTION login(username, password)  \n    READ users.txt INTO users (FORMAT: username|password|email)  \n    IF username IN users AND users[username][\'password\'] == password  \n        SET current_user = username  \n        WRITE username|timestamp TO sessions.txt  \n        RETURN True  \n    ELSE  \n        RETURN False  \n    ENDIF  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /login (POST)  \n    username = FORM[\'username\']  \n    password = FORM[\'password\']  \n    IF login(username, password)  \n        SET session[\'username\'] = username  \n        REDIRECT TO /home  \n    ELSE  \n        REDIRECT TO /login  \n    ENDIF  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` (session management, routing)  \n- File I/O for storing user sessions (`sessions.txt`)\n\n2. |Case|:user_registration\n```\nFUNCTION register(username, password, email)  \n    READ users.txt INTO users  \n    IF username IN users  \n        RETURN False  \n    ELSE  \n        APPEND username|password|email TO users.txt  \n        RETURN True  \n    ENDIF  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /register (POST)  \n    username = FORM[\'username\']  \n    password = FORM[\'password\']  \n    email = FORM[\'email\']  \n    IF register(username, password, email)  \n        REDIRECT TO /login  \n    ELSE  \n        REDIRECT TO /register  \n    ENDIF  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- File I/O (`users.txt`) for storing credentials\n\n```\nFUNCTION register(username, password)  \n    OPEN users.txt IN APPEND MODE  \n    WRITE username|password TO FILE  \n    REDIRECT TO login_page  \nEND FUNCTION  \n\n# HTML Form (register.html)  \n<form method="POST" action="/register">  \n    <input type="text" name="username" required>  \n    <input type="password" name="password" required>  \n    <button type="submit">Register</button>  \n</form>  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask`: Handles HTTP requests and form submissions.  \n- File I/O: Stores user credentials in plaintext\n\n3. ', "|Case|:view_available_items\n```\nFUNCTION read_items()  \n    READ items.txt INTO items (JSON format per line)  \n    RETURN items  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /home  \n    IF session['username'] NOT SET  \n        REDIRECT TO /login  \n    ELSE  \n        query = GET['query']  \n        items = read_items()  \n        IF query  \n            FILTER items WHERE name OR description CONTAINS query  \n        ENDIF  \n        RENDER home.html WITH items  \n    ENDIF  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `json` for parsing item data\n\n```\nFUNCTION get_items()  \n    READ items.txt  \n    FOR EACH line IN file:  \n        SPLIT line INTO id, title, description, price, seller  \n        APPEND item_data TO items_list  \n    RETURN items_list  \nEND FUNCTION  \n\n# HTML (home.html)  \n<ul>  \n    {% for item in items %}  \n        <li>{{ item.title }} - ${{ item.price }}</li>  \n    {% endfor %}  \n</ul>  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` + `Jinja2`: Renders dynamic HTML with item data\n\n4. |Case|:search_items_by_name\n```\nFUNCTION search_items(query)  \n    items = read_items()  \n    IF query  \n        RETURN items WHERE name OR description CONTAINS query (case-insensitive)  \n    ELSE  \n        RETURN items  \n    ENDIF  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /home  \n    query = GET['query']  \n    items = search_items(query)  \n    RENDER home.html WITH items  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- String operations for case-insensitive search\n\n5. ", '|Case|:view_item_details\n```\nFUNCTION get_item_details(item_id)  \n    items = read_items()  \n    RETURN items WHERE id == item_id  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /item/<item_id>  \n    IF session[\'username\'] NOT SET  \n        REDIRECT TO /login  \n    ELSE  \n        item = get_item_details(item_id)  \n        IF item NOT FOUND  \n            REDIRECT TO /home  \n        ELSE  \n            RENDER item.html WITH item  \n        ENDIF  \n    ENDIF  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- Flask dynamic routing (`/item/<item_id>`)\n\n6. |Case|:create_new_listing\n```\nFUNCTION add_item(name, description, price)  \n    item_id = timestamp + random_number  \n    item = {  \n        id: item_id,  \n        name: name,  \n        description: description,  \n        price: price,  \n        seller: current_user  \n    }  \n    APPEND item (JSON) TO items.txt  \n    RETURN True  \nENDFUNCTION  \n\nROUTE /listing (POST)  \n    IF session[\'username\'] NOT SET  \n        REDIRECT TO /login  \n    ELSE  \n        name = FORM[\'name\']  \n        description = FORM[\'description\']  \n        price = FORM[\'price\']  \n        add_item(name, description, price)  \n        REDIRECT TO /home  \n    ENDIF  \nENDROUTE  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `time` + `random` for unique ID generation  \n- `json` for storing item data\n\n```\nFUNCTION add_item(title, description, price, seller)  \n    READ items.txt TO GET existing_items  \n    new_id = LENGTH(existing_items) + 1  \n    APPEND new_id|title|description|price|seller TO items.txt  \n    REDIRECT TO home_page  \nEND FUNCTION  \n\n# HTML (listing.html)  \n<form method="POST" action="/listing">  \n    <input type="text" name="title" required>  \n    <textarea name="description" required></textarea>  \n    <input type="number" name="price" required>  \n    <button type="submit">Submit</button>  \n</form>  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask`: Processes form data and updates `items.txt`\n\n7. ', '|Case|:submit_item_listing\nSame as create_new_listing\n\n8. |Case|:navigate_back_to_home\n```\nROUTE /home  \n    RENDER home.html  \nENDROUTE  \n\n<!-- item.html -->  \n<a href="/home">Back to Home</a>  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- Flask routing + HTML navigation\n\n```\n# HTML (item_details.html)  \n<a href="/">Back to Home</a>  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- Basic HTML hyperlink (no special libraries)']
