## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:data_storage
Failure/Error Analysis1: `NoSuchElementException` when trying to find "Add New Listing" link.
Improvement Guidance1: Ensure `/home` route renders only after all data is loaded. Consider adding a loading state in `home.html` if data fetching is slow. Verify `session['username']` is correctly set before rendering `/home`. If `items.txt` is large, consider caching item data in memory for faster access.

Failure/Error Analysis2: New listing not appearing after submission.
Improvement Guidance2: Verify `add_item()` correctly appends to `items.txt`. Ensure form submission (`/listing` route) performs redirect. Use atomic writes to prevent file corruption.

2. |Case|:user_login
Failure/Error Analysis1: Login redirect fails (stays on login page).
Improvement Guidance1: Ensure `app.secret_key` is properly set. Verify session storage (Flask sessions rely on client-side cookies). Debug login flow: Check if `user_manager.login()` returns `True` before redirect.

Failure/Error Analysis2: All failing tests fail at the login step due to `TimeoutException` when waiting for the `/home` page.
Improvement Guidance2: Modify `AuthManager.is_logged_in()` to check both `sessions.txt` and Flask's `session`. Ensure `login()` updates both `session` and `sessions.txt` atomically. Add debug logs to verify redirects.

